  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Civilsamh&#xe4;llesfond Sydsudan (CSF)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Sudan Civil Society Facility (CSF) - South Sudan Civil Society Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A multi-donor fund (NL, NO, SE), managed by the Netherlands,  to support civil society in South Sudan. The Theory of Change takes into account that building a vibrant civil society in South Sudan will take time.  If sufficient investment in capacity development and core support is provided to civil society, organisations will become more effective, build sustainable relationships with the groups they represent at local level, and cooperate in networks and through dialogue to contribute to political and social change at local and/or national level. In this way, civil society will in the end be able to influence governance in South Sudan as a whole.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen avser st&#xf6;d till South Sudan Civil Society Fund (CSF), 2016-2020. 

F&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringsteorin tar h&#xe4;nsyn till att arbetet med att bygga ett livskraftigt civilsamh&#xe4;lle i Sydsudan kommer att ta tid. Det f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;tter att om tillr&#xe4;ckliga investeringar i kapacitetsutveckling och k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d ges till det civila samh&#xe4;llet, kommer organisationerna att bli mer effektiva, bygga h&#xe5;llbara relationer till de grupper som de f&#xf6;retr&#xe4;der p&#xe5; lokal niv&#xe5; och samarbeta i n&#xe4;tverk och genom dialog f&#xf6;r att bidra till politisk och social f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndring p&#xe5; lokal och/eller nationell niv&#xe5;. P&#xe5; s&#xe5; s&#xe4;tt kommer civila samh&#xe4;llet att kunna p&#xe5;verka samh&#xe4;llsstyrningen i Sydsudan som helhet. CSF kom d&#xe4;rf&#xf6;r att bidra till f&#xf6;ljande resultat: i) civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer (CSO:er) uppvisar st&#xe4;rkt organisatorisk kapacitet, ii) CSO:er bygger och f&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rker relationen till befolkningen p&#xe5; lokal niv&#xe5;, iii) CSO:er samarbetar i n&#xe4;tverk p&#xe5; distrikts-, provinsiell och nationell niv&#xe5;, och iv) CSO:er arbetar med regering i policy och beslutsfattande p&#xe5; olika niv&#xe5;er. 

Sverige och Norge finansierade CSF genom ett delegerat partnerskap (Nordic+) med Nederl&#xe4;nderna (NL), som &#xe4;r ledande givare (lead donor).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aimsed at strengthening the capacities of civil society organisations (CSOs) in South Sudan to meet the needs and rights of their constituencies through improved modes of working, cooperation and constructive engagement with the government.

The objective, as presented in theTheory of Change (ToC), was to promote inclusive and responsive decision making, leading to positive changes in the well-being of South Sudanese communities. To achieve this longterm outcome, key decision-makers need to implement policies that respond to the needs of the community and for this to happen, communities need to have an influencing power. CSF&apos;s ToC assumed that CSOs need to play an active role,
engaging relevant stakeholders for the creation of constructive solutions.

The project&apos;s two intermediate outcomes were: 
1. Changes in knowledge, behaviour, practices, and policies from key decision-makers.
2. Individual communities and groups affected by the programme have greater
capacity to act on issues that affect them.</narrative>
  </description>
